e] [17592186427517 1077 "selection" 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427517 1078 #edb/ref 17592186427507 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427517 1079 #uuid "6fb0a0b4-de3e-5b7b-8384-6969878cf78c" 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427518 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427517 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427518 1069 "q-163034" 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427518 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427518 1071 "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={e}^{xy},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427518 1072 #uuid "f77fb21a-c8bd-5017-9b85-73935660c6a9" 13194139534605 17592186045417 true] [17592186427518 1074 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})=y{e}^{xy}, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})=x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534605 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-43e47057-a760-57db-a3bf-60ce0300791b" 17592186427507 "answer-52ae776e-08b3-54b7-a885-e9217261d1b0" 17592186427508 "answer-595978fe-cf25-5127-9b94-47cb53657dd6" 17592186427509 "answer-87f84105-a6a8-5b4c-a4a3-205cfc0c3ca1" 17592186427510 "answer-9d3b2b1d-700e-5b18-891c-7521d97ad052" 17592186427511 "answer-b0cb1f9c-4d73-5f31-bf65-3a70242b80f2" 17592186427512 "answer-b28b947e-e099-5a84-a1f1-e49c76339f4d" 17592186427513 "answer-ce8a1cde-3900-5ec2-8cba-bd78da711720" 17592186427514 "answer-d60b9746-1d9b-5db9-b9ad-a63af5daaf53" 17592186427515 "answer-f3204833-987c-5155-a299-7bcc45208ed9" 17592186427516 "answer-field-6fb0a0b4-de3e-5b7b-8384-6969878cf78c" 17592186427517 "question-f77fb21a-c8bd-5017-9b85-73935660c6a9" 17592186427518}}
